# 10. STAFF NOTIFICATION DELIVERY

The notification system should be designed so that:

1. Customer places order.
2. Backend validates the order.
3. Backend saves the order.
4. Backend sends SMS notification to all configured staff numbers.
5. New order appears in staff dashboard.
6. Any available/on-duty staff member can accept it.

Avoid creating duplicate orders if multiple staff members click ACCEPT simultaneously.

The backend must guarantee that only ONE staff member can successfully claim an order.

Example:

Staff A clicks ACCEPT.

Staff B clicks ACCEPT at almost the same time.

Only one request succeeds.

The other staff member should receive:

> This order has already been accepted by another staff member.

