# 20. FIVE-MINUTE ACCEPTANCE TIMEOUT

A staff member has a maximum of **5 minutes** to accept a pending order.

The countdown begins when the order is successfully created.

Example:

Order placed at:

14:32

Acceptance deadline:

14:37

If ANY staff member accepts the order before the five-minute deadline:

PENDING
→ ORDER CONFIRMED

The five-minute timeout must be enforced by the backend/server, not only by a frontend countdown timer.

This is important because users can close their browser.

---

# 21. AUTOMATIC CANCELLATION

If NO staff member accepts the order within five minutes:

PENDING
→ CANCELLED

The customer should receive a simple message:

